{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GwC1J4JnXwdp4Kp82WXvu2","type":"tool_result","content":"212 reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped:\nchain.json\nmastery\nmeta.json\nsingle_solve\nsolver\ntime_trial\nworker-ratchet_log-local-20261015T210656.log\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/mastery:\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlast_timed.json\nlog.jsonl\nsubmissions.jsonl\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve:\nartifacts\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\ninbox.jsonl\nlog.jsonl\nstart.json\nsubmissions.jsonl\ntriage.md\nwork\nworker-single-local-20261015T210014.log\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve/artifacts:\n20261015T130023Z\nlatest\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve/artifacts/20261015T130023Z:\nevidence.zip\nmanifest.json\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve/work:\nextracted\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve/work/extracted:\nevidence\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence:\nd01--variant-000.elf\nd02--variant-000.elf\nd03--variant-000.dll\nd03--variant-000.runtimeconfig.json\nd04--variant-000.elf\nd05--variant-000.elf\nd06--variant-000.jar\nd06--variant-000_x\nd07--variant-000.jar\nd07--variant-000_x\nd08--variant-000.elf\nd09--variant-000.elf\nd10--variant-000.elf\nd11--variant-000.elf\nd12--variant-000.elf\nd13--variant-000.elf\nd14--variant-000.elf\nd15--variant-000-stripped.elf\nd15--variant-000-symbolized.elf\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d06--variant-000_x:\nDay06Variant000$Result.class\nDay06Variant000.class\nMETA-INF\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d06--variant-000_x/META-INF:\nMANIFEST.MF\n\nchallenges/day15/binary-stripped/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d07--variant-000_x:\nDay07Variant000$main$1.class\nDay07Variant000$main$2.class\nDay07Variant000$staged$1.class\nDay07Variant000.class\nMETA-INF\nResult.class\nkotlin\n\n# binary-swift-justice solver notes\n\nVARIANT AXIS: Mastery set count (2 on auto-mastery-d1a6613c, up to 5 x 31 MB on D8) -- main() now groups (answer_id, question) pairs with lib.common.group_by_set and solves each set in a fork ProcessPoolExecutor (sequential fallback on pool error, HCTF_SOLVER_PARALLEL=0 disables); each set's delivery is still paired by contract sha256 via container_by_sha. Output identical to the sequential loop on all 9 cases.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only (no answer change) -- the evidence.zip is all WinZip AE-2 (method 99, AES-256, deflate) and its 67 MB d08 Swift ELF was inflated serially through pyzipper (pure-Python HMAC-SHA1 + AES); unzip() now reads AES members directly (PBKDF2 + AES-CTR LE counter, pw-verifier check, no HMAC) in a thread pool, largest first, decrypt||inflate||sha256 pipelined for members > 8 MB, and returns Futures that group_members() resolves only for the group asked (falls back to the pyzipper reader on any miss). single 1.2 s -> 0.8 s local.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only (no answer change; the 9.74 s was the harness's contention-measured Mastery estimate, real single = 0.5-0.6 s, 5-set Mastery 1.7-1.9 s pinned to 2 CPUs) -- per-set CPU trimmed: AE-2 members (CRC 0) skip the 67 MB crc32 pass, multi-set runs inflate the big member in one shot instead of the 3-thread pipeline (+20% CPU, ~0 wall), and the lazy deps (capstone/pefile/Cryptodome/lib.common) import once in the parent before forking. Floor: stock zlib inflate of the 67 MB d08 Swift ELF = 0.2 s/set.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only, no code change (D12 single re-flagged at 8.49 s = harness contention, load avg ~6) -- measured single 0.90 s wall pinned to 2 CPUs (in-process 0.65 s), 5-set Mastery 1.3 s wall / 5.8 s CPU; critical path = inflate of the 67 MB d08 Swift member (0.35 s, single deflate stream, sha256 of it is asked so it cannot be skipped) + AES 0.08 + sha 0.06 + HCFG scan 0.07; imports 0.25 s (capstone already lazy). All 17 cases pass.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.fast_aes_unzip(data, passwords)` -> [(name, Future[bytes])] + sha256 cache: the `_aes_member` / `_fast_unzip` pair in day09 binary-nimble solve.py (WinZip AE-x without pyzipper's pure-Python HMAC pass; zlib/pycryptodome/hashlib release the GIL so members inflate in parallel). Every lane whose evidence.zip carries a large member benefits.\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no answer change) the \"8.21s on single_solve\" flag was CPU contention from parallel solver-tests, not the solver: isolated it runs 0.55-0.60 s wall on the single (taskset 2 vCPUs, ~0.75 s CPU) and 1.2 s on a 3-set Mastery; critical path is the d08 67 MB Swift member's AES-CTR||inflate||sha256 pipeline (done at ~0.37 s) + ~0.09 s of field analysis -- measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...`, not under a loaded solver-test.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D14) the \"4.11 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.51 s wall (0.6 s unpinned; the harness cProfile itself shows 0.048 s for import), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-7439276e 1.42 s wall pinned / 0.80 s unpinned; all 21 cases pass with every answer_id filled. Nothing to trim that the earlier cycles have not already trimmed.\n{\n  \"55988fa5-8263-4820-bc08-44f1d8fc2a9e\": {\n    \"d01_artifact_sha256_1\": \"a0d3aeddb90dccf579e0262704dc7d7c2828121d8cc988f085de169601737b9b\",\n    \"d01_analysis_elf_class\": \"ELF64\",\n    \"d01_analysis_machine\": \"x86-64\",\n    \"d01_analysis_section_names\": \"[\\\"\\\",\\\".interp\\\",\\\".note.gnu.property\\\",\\\".note.ABI-tag\\\",\\\".hash\\\",\\\".gnu.hash\\\",\\\".dynsym\\\",\\\".dynstr\\\",\\\".gnu.version\\\",\\\".gnu.version_r\\\",\\\".rela.dyn\\\",\\\".init\\\",\\\".text\\\",\\\".fini\\\",\\\".rodata\\\",\\\".huntress\\\",\\\".eh_frame_hdr\\\",\\\".eh_frame\\\",\\\".init_array\\\",\\\".fini_array\\\",\\\".dynamic\\\",\\\".got\\\",\\\".got.plt\\\",\\