r field d01_artifact_sha256_1 in the delivered evidence set?\",\n      \"artifact\": \"evidence.zip\",\n      \"answer_format\": {\n        \"kind\": \"exact_text\",\n        \"syntax\": \"exact artifact-derived value only, without quotes or explanatory text unless quotes are part of the value; use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\"\n      },\n      \"normalization\": \"exact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d01_analysis_elf_class\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the exact analysis elf class value for field d01_analysis_elf_class in the delivered evidence set?\",\n      \"artifact\": \"evidence.zip\",\n      \"answer_format\": {\n        \"kind\": \"exact_text\",\n        \"syntax\": \"exact artifact-derived value only, without quotes or explanatory text unless quotes are part of the value; use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\"\n      },\n      \"normalization\": \"exact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d01_analysis_machine\",\n      \"question\": \"For the requested delivered binary, report the processor architecture identified by its executable-header machine field. A normalized architecture name, a standard tool or symbolic label, or the equivalent decimal or hexadecimal machine code is accepted.\",\n      \"artifact\": \"evidence.zip\",\n      \"answer_format\": {\n        \"kind\": \"pattern\",\n        \"syntax\": \"executable-header machine architecture label or its equivalent decimal or hexadecimal code; common file, readelf, and objdump labels are accepted\"\n      },\n      \"normalization\": \"exact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d01_analysis_section_names\",\n      \"question\": \"For the bundled Day 1 ELF, submit the section names in section-header-table order as a JSON array of strings. The mandatory null section at index 0 has an empty name; including or omitting that one leading empty string is accepted. Do not substitute the section type NULL for its empty name.\",\n      \"artifact\": \"evidence.zip\",\n      \"answer_format\": {\n        \"kind\": \"json\",\n        \"syntax\": \"JSON array of section-name strings in section-header-table order; an optional leading empty string represents section index 0\"\n      },\n      \"normalization\": \"exact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d01_analysis_symbols\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the exact analysis symbols value for field d01_analysis_symbols in the delivered evidence set?\",\n      \"artifact\": \"evidence.zip\",\n      \"answer_format\": {\n        \"kind\": \"json\",\n        \"syntax\": \"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order; no Markdown or explanatory text\"\n      },\n      \"normalization\": \"exact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d01_analysis_disassembly\",\n      \"question\": \"In the bundled Day 1 ELF, find the recover_code FUNC symbol in the symbol table and disassemble its bytes. Submit its decoded instructions in execution order as a JSON array of strings, without addresses or byte columns. If that symbol is absent, submit []. Unrelated format example: [\\\"nop\\\",\\\"ret\\\"].\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GwC1J4JnXwdp4Kp82WXvu2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
